   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Collocations with tage and få",
     "texto": [
      "With **tage** (to take) one says **tage en beslutning** (to make a decision) and **tage en pause** (to take a break). With **få** (to get) one says **få en idé** (to have an idea): **Jeg fik en god idé.** = A good idea came to me."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Collocations with gøre and lave",
     "texto": [
      "With **gøre** (to do): **gøre rent** (to clean), **gøre en indsats** (to make an effort). With **lave** (to make, to prepare): **lave mad** (to cook), **lave lektier** (to do homework).",
      "Careful: in English we use «do» and «make» for lots of things, but in Danish each verb has its own expression."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
